  "description": "Which moment actually sells Pro (SPEC §14)?\n\n**The honest answer is: this board cannot fully say yet.** `iap.paywall_shown` carries the `trigger` that opened it; `iap.purchase_result` carries only `outcome` and `error_kind`. So the offer side splits by moment and the buy side does not, and conversion is a single blended number. Adding `trigger` to the purchase event is the one change that would make this board answer its own question — see `docs/practices/app-events.md`.\n\n**Refusals emit nothing.** An offer the coordinator declined — capped, disabled, already Pro — produces no event, so `iap.paywall_shown` is the offer rate and not the attempt rate. The ratio of it to `ads.gate_shown` is on this board as 'Offer rate'.\n\n**Loki-backed, so nothing here can see past Grafana Cloud's log retention.** Widening the time picker does not widen the answer.\n\n**Delivery is at-least-once.** A record can rarely ship twice (export acknowledged, process died before the buffer delete), so read raw counts as approximate. Panels that count *installs* rather than records are immune to it by construction — a duplicate lands in the same `install_id` series and collapses.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 0,
  "links": [],
